        "topic": "Internal Combustion Engine Cycles",
        "question_type": "Practical",
        "exam_year": "2016",
        "question_text": "<p>In a four-stroke petrol engine, identify the correct sequence of the following events:<br>(i) Power stroke<br>(ii) Exhaust stroke<br>(iii) Intake stroke<br>(iv) Compression stroke</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>The correct sequence of events in a four-stroke petrol engine is:<br>(1) <b>Intake stroke</b>: Air-fuel mixture is drawn into the cylinder.<br>(2) <b>Compression stroke</b>: The mixture is compressed.<br>(3) <b>Power stroke</b>: The spark plug ignites the mixture, forcing the piston down.<br>(4) <b>Exhaust stroke</b>: Burnt gases are expelled from the cylinder.<br>The correct order is (iii), (iv), (i), (ii).</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "64787",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "(i), (ii), (iii), (iv)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "85689",
                "tag": "b",
                "text": "(iii), (iv), (i), (ii)",
                "is_correct": true
            },
            {
                "option_id": "27687",
                "tag": "c",
                "text": "(iv), (iii), (ii), (i)",
                "is_correct": false
            },
            {
                "option_id": "13684",
                "tag": "d",
                "text": "(ii), (i), (iv), (iii)",
                "is_correct": false
            }
        ],
